  "rationale": "Two of the three added columns (is_processed, days_to_process) cohere tightly around a single, data-inferable focus: expense processing efficiency/latency, which is genuinely actionable (identify unprocessed items and extreme-latency outliers). These are not mere restatements -- days_to_process derives a meaningful metric from processed_date/opened_at and surfaces investigable anomalies. However, amount_decile introduces a second, distinct concept (spend magnitude) that is not obviously part of the same processing focus, making the set read partly as a small grab-bag rather than a unified facet decomposition around one focus. Structure is sound but thin (only a couple of coherent facets plus a stray dimension), and the deciles column is a mechanical binning rather than a targeted facet. Actionability is solid for the processing angle but diluted by the mixed framing."
}
